Subject: [PATCH 2/2] The embedded request builder has no vendor promotion in its empty response panel

Why: before a request is sent, the response panel of the modal layout shows a "Powered by scalar.com" link and a large ASCII-art
computer. The modal is the only layout the engine uses, inside an app's own documentation page, where neither belongs (and the
link is the one outbound link in the panel). The other layouts keep both, as upstream has them.

Touches: packages/api-client ResponseEmpty.vue only (two v-if attributes).

---
diff --git a/packages/api-client/src/v2/blocks/response-block/components/ResponseEmpty.vue b/packages/api-client/src/v2/blocks/response-block/components/ResponseEmpty.vue
index c0076b3..8a6b6d6 100644
--- a/packages/api-client/src/v2/blocks/response-block/components/ResponseEmpty.vue
+++ b/packages/api-client/src/v2/blocks/response-block/components/ResponseEmpty.vue
@@ -47,12 +47,14 @@ const { translate } = useLocalization()
         </div>
       </div>
       <a
+        v-if="layout !== 'modal'"
         class="gitbook-show scalar-version-number"
         href="https://www.scalar.com"
         target="_blank"
         >{{ translate('apiClient.responseEmpty.poweredByScalarcom') }}</a
       >
       <ScalarAsciiArt
+        v-if="layout !== 'modal'"
         :art="Computer"
         class="text-c-3" />
     </div>
